❓Question
Given an integer array nums, move all 0s to the end while maintaining the relative order of the non-zero elements.
You must do it in-place, without making a copy of the array.

Example
Input:
nums = [0,1,0,3,12]
Output:
[1,3,12,0,0]
Input:
nums = [0]
Output:
[0]

✅Approach
Use two pointers:
p2 scans the entire array.
p1 points to the position where the next non-zero element should go.
Whenever nums[p2] != 0, swap nums[p1] and nums[p2].
Then increase p1.
This automatically pushes all zeroes toward the end while keeping non-zero elements in their original order.

Code
class Solution {
    public void moveZeroes(int[] nums) {
        int p1 = 0;
        for(int p2 = 0; p2 < nums.length; p2++) {
            if(nums[p2] != 0) {
                int temp = nums[p1];
                nums[p1] = nums[p2];
                nums[p2] = temp;
                p1++;
            }
        }
    }
}
Time Complexity
O(n)
Space Complexity
O(1)
